                <head>No. 356<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>Following the fourth formal meeting with President Truman, Prime Minister Churchill went to New York, January
                    9–11, and then to Ottawa for discussions with the Canadians, January 12–15. A
                    report on the talks in Canada is in telegram 114, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >infra</hi>. The Prime Minister then returned to Washington, January 16–18,
                    to address a joint session of Congress on January 17 and for a final meeting
                    with President Truman, January 18.
                    For a record of this final meeting, see <ref target="#d359">Document
                    359</ref>.</p>
                <p>Foreign Secretary Eden remained in
                    Washington until January 10 before leaving for New York where he made an address
                    at Columbia University the next day. Eden stayed in New York 4 more days before flying back to the
                    United Kingdom on January 15.</p>
            </div>
